    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Monday, January 14, 2019 at 6:23:31 PM UTC+11, Craig Marsh wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">If you are using that vector container just for use in a logical condition I would suggest avoiding strings and going with int, I have added what I mean in the following code (disclaimer I haven&#39;t compiled or run the code).<div><div><pre style=\"background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,74,67)\">#</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,74,67)\">include </span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(64,1,90)\">TMB.hpp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0)\">&gt;</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">template</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&lt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">class</span> Type<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&gt;</span>\r\nType objective_function<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&lt;</span>Type<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&gt;</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">::</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">operator</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">{</span>\r\n  DATA_MATRIX<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>mZ<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  DATA_MATRIX<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>mY<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105)\">// Use a vector of ints</span>\r\n  DATA_IVECTOR<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>types<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(105,105,105)\">// 1 = Type 1, 2 = Type 2 etc ...</span>\r\n  PARAMETER_MATRIX<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>vu<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  \r\n  matrix<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&lt;</span>Type<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&gt;</span> m1 <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> mZ<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">*</span>vu\r\n    \r\n  matrix<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&lt;</span>Type<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">&gt;</span> m2 <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">log</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">exp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>m1<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">array</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">+</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  \r\n  Type l <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> types<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">.</span>size<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  \r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">int</span> j <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span> j <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">&lt;</span> l<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">+</span>j<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">{</span>\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">if</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>types<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">[</span>j<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">]</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">{</span>\r\n      m2<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>j<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">exp</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>m1<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">.</span><span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">array</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>j<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n    <span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">}</span>\r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">}</span>\r\n  \r\n  Type nll <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> m2<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span>\r\n  \r\n  <span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,0);font-weight:bold\">return</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>nll<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">;</span> \r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128)\">}</span>\r\n\r\n\r\ntmb_dat <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(96,48,0)\">list</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span>\r\n  types <span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">=</span> c<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">,</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,140,0)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span>\r\n<span style=\"color:rgb(128,128,48)\">)</span>\r\n</pre>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n</pre></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Jan 14, 2019 at 7:09 PM Aaron Greenberg &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jaguar...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">You probably can do something like the attached.... but I don&#39;t know I fully understand the question. <div>Aaron</div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Sun, Jan 13, 2019 at 9:31 PM &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">sarah....@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<div><br></div><div>First time poster here! </div><div><br></div><div>Sorry if this is a basic question, but I can&#39;t seem to figure out how to use the C++ macros to code up the equivalent of a vector of strings in R, such as</div><div><br></div><div>names = c(&quot;Type 1&quot;, &quot;Type 2&quot;, &quot;Type 1&quot;).</div><div><br></div><div>I tried DATA_STRING(), but I don&#39;t think this is giving me what I would like. So I&#39;m trying DATA_VECTOR but I think this is also incorrect.</div><div><br></div><div>An example is here below - I would like to change the jth value of m2 depending on whether the jth value of names is either &quot;Type 1&quot; or Type 2&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>###############################</div><div><br></div><div><div>#include &lt;TMB.hpp&gt;</div><div>template&lt;class Type&gt;</div><div>  Type objective_function&lt;Type&gt;::operator() ()</div><div>{</div><div><div>  DATA_MATRIX(mZ);</div><div>  DATA_MATRIX(mY);</div></div><div>  DATA_VECTOR(names);</div><div>  PARAMETER_MATRIX(vu);</div><div><br></div><div>  matrix&lt;Type&gt; m1 = mZ*vu</div><div>  </div><div>  matrix&lt;Type&gt; m2 = log(exp(m1.array()) + 1);</div><div>  </div><div>  Type l = names.size();</div><div>  </div><div>  for(int j = 0; j &lt; l; j = j + 1){</div><div>    std::string val = <a href=\"http://names.at\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://names.at&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462380095000&amp;usg=AOvVaw241RoGzSh4LKIwCyR90BOv\">names.at</a>(j);</div><div>    if(val!=&quot;Type 1&quot;){</div><div>      m2(j)= exp(m1.array()(j));</div><div>    }</div><div>  }</div><div>  </div><div>  Type nll = m2(0);</div><div>  </div><div>  return(nll); </div><div>  }</div></div><div><br></div><div>###############################</div><div><br></div><div>There are probably many other issues with my code as well - sorry!</div><div><br></div><div>Any help at all will be much appreciated!</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers</div><div>Sarah</div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">us...@tmb-project.org</a>. Before posting, please check the wiki and issuetracker at <a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462380095000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iyLEmVSzDT_sIaSPqOZUf\">https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/</a>. Please try to create a simple repeatable example to go with your question (e.g issues 154, 134, 51). Use the issuetracker to report bugs.<br>\r\n--- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;TMB Users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">tmb-users+...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57b52bd0-7846-405a-8710-21e926c9025f%40googlegroups.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57b52bd0-7846-405a-8710-21e926c9025f%2540googlegroups.com?utm_medium%3Demail%26utm_source%3Dfooter&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462380095000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16xh87Nkn6n1QkWMFAfTZk\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/tmb-users/57b52bd0-7846-405a-8710-21e926c9025f%40googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nFor more options, visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/optout\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/optout&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462380095000&amp;usg=AOvVaw08hFVHqymMwiEVkLM8EPKQ\">https://groups.google.com/d/optout</a>.<br>\r\n</blockquote></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">us...@tmb-project.org</a>. Before posting, please check the wiki and issuetracker at <a href=\"https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462380095000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1iyLEmVSzDT_sIaSPqOZUf\">https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/</a>. Please try to create a simple repeatable example to go with your question (e.g issues 154, 134, 51). Use the issuetracker to report bug